        "Around those dates, Sanand has its own rhythm. Navratri in Sharad is the point at which serious study stops for most of Gujarat, and nine nights of garba is not a cultural footnote but a genuine scheduling fact. Diwali and the new year that follows it close everything again, Uttarayan in mid-January takes a weekend out for kite flying, and Holi marks the start of the final run towards May papers.",
